# BUGS

A loop freed while one of its I/O threads waits in a held read (the console, a pipe) leaves that thread to finish, its stack mapped.
`vx_watch` on `VX_STDIN` works when it is a pipe, not the console; on a file of a server dialled over TCP it is `VX_ERR_UNSUPPORTED`.
`vx_rename` within one directory of a server without the posix extension removes what is at <to> first, so it is not atomic there.
